              <details>
                <summary>Where people get lost</summary>
                <ul class="pitfalls">
                  <li><b>Manual migrations that get skipped</b> — run migrations as an explicit deploy step so production schema can't silently drift from what the code expects.</li>
                  <li><b>No monitoring, so failures are only found when a user reports them</b> — even the free tier of a basic error tracker beats finding out from a support email.</li>
                </ul>
              </details>

              <details>
                <summary>Checkpoint project</summary>
                <p class="checkpoint">The task tracker deployed to a free host with a managed free Postgres database, live and reachable end-to-end, with migrations running automatically on deploy.</p>
              </details>
            </div>
